 // Hunt widths: [hunt monster] rows are [dungeon, difficulty threshold, monster, goal] (width 4);
 // [hunt enemy] rows add an enemy type discriminator before the goal, so width 5 and the goal is
 // the last column. Deliberate, still-unproven deviation recorded on purpose: the enemy type column
 // is NOT used as a kill gate. rednf reads m_enemyType only in the [monster/enemy reward item] drop
 // path (CheckKillMonster.inc) and its ENUM_QUEST_ENEMY_TYPE is a placeholder stub (Quest.h), while
 // the original decrements the objective counter from the client trigger (opcode 0x23), so no static
 // evidence settles an objective gate on it. We match on monster id alone until a dynamic capture
 // proves otherwise; see local-run/recon/hunt-enemy-spec.md sections 1, 4 and 6. New static evidence
 // (local-run/recon/hunt-enemy-missing-monsters.md) narrows that: rows with enemy type 3 point at
 // destructible passive objects (d31 shallowkeep [special passive object]), not at .mob ids, so
 // monster-id matching can never credit them and those rows must stay unsupported until an
 // object-kill path exists. APC-shaped targets ([ai character] rows) are likewise uncredited:
 // Batch-Service-FG.cs:156 routes APC/GSD deaths into the Act4 boss-apc branch, which never reaches
 // the quest kill feed at :160.
